00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:13.212
-Okay, so it's 8:30
in the morning.

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:14.780
Why am I awake?

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:19.051
I sort of unexpectedly started
writing an album,

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:23.623
and I just felt really inspired
and I went with it.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:29.429
And I recorded an entire album
with The Roots remotely.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:36.769
♪♪

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:38.004
Cheers!

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.373
This is so wild!

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.475
You know,
when lockdown first started,

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.577
I heard Taylor
was writing songs,

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:47.113
and I thought
I was feeling inspired too,

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.081
so maybe I should
write some music.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:51.817
I remember I called you, Tariq,
and I asked if you'd help me.

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:53.019
And you said --

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:55.488
-"Only if you pay me
a lot of money."

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.655
-Exactly.

00:00:56.655 --> 00:00:58.558
And, Quest, I texted you,
and I said,

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.693
"Hey, do you want to work on
something together?"

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:01.961
And you said --

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.596
-"How did you get this number?"

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.232
-Yeah, but actually,
I was getting pretty bored,

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:09.469
so I said, "Okay."

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:13.873
-It's just a lot of the themes
in my songs

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.708
are hard to talk about.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.410
But I know other people
are probably

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.912
going through the same things.
-Yeah.

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:23.049
-So maybe the music will
resonate with them.

